REPEATABLE READ Isolation Level

Objective: To demonstrate how PostgreSQL maintains a consistent snapshot throughout a transaction.

Scenario: Two PostgreSQL sessions accessed the same CampusCart product record.

Session A: Started a REPEATABLE READ transaction and retrieved the product stock as 24.

Session B: Increased the product stock by one unit and committed the change. The updated stock became 25.

Observation: When Session A executed the SELECT statement again, it continued displaying 24 rather than 25.

Conclusion: PostgreSQL REPEATABLE READ ensures that repeated queries within the same transaction see a consistent snapshot of the database, even when another transaction commits changes.
